[gd_scene load_steps=29 format=3]

; Mounted single-disc fertilizer spreader (broadcaster). Authored in the LOWERED (working)
; pose with the origin ON THE LOWER PIN LINE, the frame HitchLinkage solves against; ground is
; y = -0.21 in this frame. Unlike the plough and the mower, NOTHING on this machine touches
; the ground at any hitch position — a spreader throws from a disc held clear of the crop, and
; that is exactly why it is not draft-relevant (see spreader.gd).
;
; The drive train is drawn the way a real single-disc machine runs it: input shaft angling
; forward and up out of the gearbox toward the tractor's PTO stub, a shaft back UNDER the
; hopper, a small bevel box under the outlet, and a short vertical shaft down into the disc.
; The telescoping driveshaft between the stub and the input shaft is not modelled (the one
; mechanical part left out on every implement).
;
; The slide GATE under the hopper outlet and the ram beside it are real parts, not decoration:
; they are what makes declaring Connection.SCV honest, and 'scv_flow' slides them (spreader.gd
; reads their AUTHORED positions as the shut pose, so moving them here moves the shut gate).
; NO CollisionShape: implements are visual.

